61 is queued to fix it. That file is outside my target, so I left it alone. The other five acceptance commands pass: the new profile script (`ok runs=5`), sdkjs-word 42/42, sdkjs-common 7/7, and both differentials.\n\n**What I did**\n- The scripts from attempts 1–3 had never been committed, so I wrote them again: `.theseus/oracle/journeys/open-docx-10p-profile.sh` and `open-docx-10p-profile-run.cjs`. They run the same journey against the integrated build with a CDP CPU profile, cut it into three windows (shell boot, client window, recalc after load complete), and attribute each window with the unchanged `perf/attribute-word.js`.\n- The run was on a quiet VM (load average about 0.5), which the earlier runs could not get.\n- `open-docx-10p.md` now uses these measured splits instead of the PKT-0043 estimate. The stages still add up to 8 340 ms.\n\n**Measured split (share of busy CPU time)**\n\n| Window | Idle | Browser | sdkjs-word | sdkjs-common | web-apps |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Client (Editor.bin → load complete) | 18 % | 40 % | 34 % | 15 % | 11 % |\n| Shell boot | 14 % | 34 % | none | 6 % | 60 % |\n| Recalc after complete | 2 % | 26 % | 32 % | 10 % | 32 % |\n\nPKT-0043 had estimated word at 41 % and the browser at 20 % of the client window. In fact the browser's own work (parse/compile, page layout and paint) is the largest single item there.\n\n**Decisions**\n- I did not re-measure the marks. I kept the earlier window lengths and split each one by the measured idle fraction and shares.\n- The web-apps time in the recalc window (234 ms) is merged into the existing `client-open-webapps-ui` stage. `validate` rejects the name `layout-finish-webapps` for web-apps stages, which is the same error the 100p file hits.\n- I added `/deploy-integrated/` again to the sdkjs checkout's local `.git/info/exclude`. The sdkjs checkout stays clean after a run and `theseus scope-check` passes.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas** (written in the packet)\n- The browser's own work is th